From f5ba5c94524ed6ca19f463499412d1aded12eb18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yami <yami@localhost>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 15:57:45 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] yami: layer rule show-only-in

The opposite of block-out-from: a layer surface matched by
show-only-in "screencast" (or "screen-capture") is drawn only to those
render targets and never on the monitor. The shell uses it for a
privacy curtain: viewers of a stream or a recording see a cover while
the user keeps seeing the desktop. The look is drawn by the shell; the
compositor only decides where the surface is shown.
